    "recommendations": "• Install a reflective address marker at the driveway entrance so responders can identify the property quickly from the road.\n• Mark the driveway entrance with posts or reflectors on both sides to define the edge for large emergency vehicles approaching at night or in low visibility.\n• Keep the full width of the driveway clear of parked vehicles, equipment, and landscaping to allow emergency vehicles to reach the residence without stopping.\n• Maintain a vehicle turnaround area near the residence so fire and medical units do not have to back out the full length of the driveway.\n• Keep a designated area of the parking surface open at all times for ambulance or fire apparatus to stage close to the front entrance.\n• Trim any landscaping along the driveway that narrows the travel width or reduces overhead clearance for taller emergency vehicles.\n• Install a gate lock box or provide a Knox-Box at the driveway entrance if a gate is present, so responders are not delayed waiting for access.\n• Identify and mark a secondary foot approach to the rear of the property so responders are not limited to the single vehicle access point if the driveway is blocked.\n• Post the property address visibly at both the road and near the residence itself to assist responders navigating the long driveway.\n• Keep a clear path on foot from the parking area to the detached structure so responders"
