    "recommendations": "• Trim tree branches that hang directly over or touch the house and any outbuildings.\n• Thin scattered trees closest to the structure to increase open space between the canopy and the building.\n• Cut grass around the structure short, especially during dry months when it dries out quickly.\n• Remove shrubs growing directly against or within a few feet of the house walls.\n• Thin or remove shrubs that are close enough to connect the fire from open terrain to the structure.\n• Keep the long driveway clear of overhanging branches so emergency vehicles can pass without obstruction.\n• Cut back vegetation along both sides of the driveway to maintain clear lines of sight and room for vehicles to move.\n• Mark the driveway entrance clearly so it is visible to emergency responders approaching from the road.\n• Remove dead or dry plant material from around the base of trees and shrubs near the structure.\n• Keep the area immediately around the structure as open as possible by pulling back scattered shrubs that have grown toward the building over time."
